he hundreds digit of the product \\(5 \\times 6 \\times 7 \\times 8 \\times 9 \\times 10\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the product**:\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 6 \\times 7 \\times 8 \\times 9 \\times 10\n   \\]\n\n2. **Simplify the multiplication step-by-step**:\n   - First, multiply \\(5\\) and \\(10\\):\n     \\[\n     5 \\times 10 = 50\n     \\]\n   - Next, multiply the result by \\(6\\):\n     \\[\n     50 \\times 6 = 300\n     \\]\n   - Then, multiply the result by \\(7\\):\n     \\[\n     300 \\times 7 = 2100\n     \\]\n   - Next, multiply the result by \\(8\\):\n     \\[\n     2100 \\times 8 = 16800\n     \\]\n   - Finally, multiply the result by \\(9\\):\n     \\[\n     16800 \\times 9 = 151200\n     \\]\n\n3. **Identify the hundreds digit**:\n   - The number \\(151200\\) can be written in the form \\(151200\\).\n   - The hundreds digit is the third digit from the right, which is \\(2\\).\n\nTherefore, the hundreds digit of the product \\(5 \\times 6 \\times 7 \\times 8 \\times 9 \\times 10\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
